  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **buenas tardes (mickey on drums, claude on guitar)** (1 review): Deaner and Claude switching places surprised everyone in the audience and sounded fantastic [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **help my pony**: rare: 13 archived performances [4]\n- **sweet tx fire**: mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n- **tear for eddie**: back after 106 archived shows (1188 days) [4]\n- **buenas tardes (mickey on drums, claude on guitar)**: back after 74 archived shows (1039 days); rare: 7 archived performances [4]\n- **l.m.l.y.p. > crimson and clover**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **ween2006-07-31.akgc1000s** (recommended): source not stated; 29 songs; 195 min; rated 4.5/5 by 2 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer stood second row near Deaner, beside a man in overalls wearing a boognish head [2]\n- Gener can be heard on the recording saying \"boognish hat\" [2]\n- The band played the whole show without taking a break [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **ween2006-07-31.akgc1000s**: taped by matt b.; transferred by matt b.; source: akg c1000s -> rolls pb224 -> sony mz-m10 (hi-sp) [1]. Also: Reviewer filmed the show and is preparing a DVD and online release of the video [3]",
